INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.disk_reservation_percent:25	- The percentage of total disk capacity that Redpanda will avoid using. This applies both when cloud cache and log data share a disk, as well as when cloud cache uses a dedicated disk. It is recommended to not run disks near capacity to avoid blocking I/O due to low disk space, as well as avoiding performance issues associated with SSD garbage collection.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.election_timeout_ms:1500ms	- Election timeout expressed in milliseconds.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_auto_rebalance_on_node_add:false	- Enable automatic partition rebalancing when new nodes are added
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_cluster_metadata_upload_loop:true	- Enables cluster metadata uploads. Required for whole cluster restore.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_consumer_group_metrics:["group", "partition"]	- List of enabled consumer group metrics. Accepted Values: `group`, `partition`, `consumer_lag`
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_controller_log_rate_limiting:false	- Limits the write rate for the controller log.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_development_metrics:false	- Enable registering development-oriented metrics on the internal `/metrics` endpoint, such as the per-method internal RPC latency histograms.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_developmental_unrecoverable_data_corrupting_features:	- Development features should never be enabled in a production cluster, or any cluster where stability, data loss, or the ability to upgrade are a concern. To enable experimental features, set the value of this configuration option to the current unix epoch expressed in seconds. The value must be within one hour of the current time on the broker. Once experimental features are enabled they cannot be disabled.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_host_metrics:true	- Enable exporting of some host metrics like /proc/diskstats, /proc/snmp and /proc/net/netstat
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_idempotence:true	- Enable idempotent producers.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_leader_balancer:true	- Enable automatic leadership rebalancing.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_listoffsets_historical_leader_epoch:false	- When enabled, the Kafka ListOffsets API returns the historical (record-time) leader epoch instead of the current leader epoch. Intended as a one-way opt-in: disabling after it has been enabled regresses to the original bug. Gated as a development feature: not all response paths are fixed yet (CORE-12505), so enabling this property produces internally inconsistent epoch values across paths and must not be enabled in production.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_metrics_reporter:true	- Enable the cluster metrics reporter. If `true`, the metrics reporter collects and exports to Redpanda Data a set of customer usage metrics at the interval set by `metrics_reporter_report_interval`. The cluster metrics of the metrics reporter are different from the monitoring metrics. * The metrics reporter exports customer usage metrics for consumption by Redpanda Data.* Monitoring metrics are exported for consumption by Redpanda users.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_mpx_extensions:false	- Enable Redpanda extensions for MPX.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_pid_file:true	- Enable PID file. You should not need to change.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_rack_awareness:false	- Enable rack-aware replica assignment.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_sasl:false	- Enable SASL authentication for Kafka connections. Authorization is required to modify this property. See also `kafka_enable_authorization`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_schema_id_validation:none	- Mode to enable server-side schema ID validation. Accepted Values: * `none`: Schema validation is disabled (no schema ID checks are done). Associated topic properties cannot be modified. * `redpanda`: Schema validation is enabled. Only Redpanda topic properties are accepted. * `compat`: Schema validation is enabled. Both Redpanda and compatible topic properties are accepted.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_shadow_linking:false	- Enable creating Shadow Links from this cluster to a remote source cluster for data replication.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_transactions:true	- Enable transactions (atomic writes).
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_usage:false	- Enables the usage tracking mechanism, storing windowed history of kafka/cloud_storage metrics over time.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.features_auto_enable:true	- Whether features whose `available_policy` is `always` or `new_clusters_only` are auto-activated by the controller after the cluster active logical version reaches their required version. When false, the cluster active version still advances normally, but each such feature must be activated explicitly via the Admin API. Does not affect features with `available_policy::explicit_only`, which always require explicit activation.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.features_auto_finalization:true	- Whether the cluster active logical version is advanced automatically once all nodes have been upgraded (true), or only in response to an explicit request via the Admin API (false). When false, the cluster remains able to downgrade to the previous version until finalization is requested. Setting this to false is an Enterprise feature and requires a valid license. Note: if upgrade was performed with this set to false and the cluster is ready to finalize, flipping this to true does not reliably trigger finalization. Leave this set to false and use the Admin API to finalize; once the upgrade is complete this can be set back to true to restore automatic finalization for future upgrades.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_max_bytes:57671680	- Maximum number of bytes returned in a fetch request.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_max_read_concurrency:1	- The maximum number of concurrent partition reads per fetch request on each shard. Setting this higher than the default can lead to partition starvation and unneeded memory usage.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_pid_d_coeff:0	- Derivative coefficient for fetch PID controller.
