INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_backlog_controller_i_coeff:0.005	- Integral coefficient for the Iceberg backlog controller. The error is integrated (accumulated) over time and the aggregated value contributes to the datalake translation priority with this coefficient.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_backlog_controller_p_coeff:1e-05	- Proportional coefficient for the Iceberg backlog controller. Number of shares assigned to the datalake scheduling group will be proportional to the backlog size error.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_base_location:redpanda-iceberg-catalog	- Base path for the cloud-storage-object-backed Iceberg filesystem catalog. After Iceberg is enabled, do not change this value.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_commit_interval_ms:60000ms	- The frequency at which the Iceberg coordinator commits topic files to the catalog. This is the interval between commit transactions across all topics monitored by the coordinator, not the interval between individual commits.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_type:object_storage	- Iceberg catalog type that Redpanda will use to commit table metadata updates. Supported types: 'rest', 'object_storage'
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_default_catalog_namespace:["redpanda"]	- The default namespace (database name) for Iceberg tables. All tables created by Redpanda will be placed in this namespace within the Iceberg catalog. Supports nested namespaces as an array of strings. IMPORTANT: This value must be configured before enabling Iceberg and must not be changed afterward. Changing it will cause Redpanda to lose track of existing tables.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_default_partition_spec:(hour(redpanda.timestamp))	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.partition.spec topic property that determines the partition spec for the Iceberg table corresponding to the topic. If this property is not set and AWS Glue is being used as the Iceberg REST catalog, the default value will be overridden by an empty partition spec, for compatibility with AWS Glue.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_delete:true	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.delete topic property that determines if the corresponding Iceberg table is deleted upon deleting the topic.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_disable_automatic_snapshot_expiry:false	- Whether to disable automatic Iceberg snapshot expiry. This may be useful if the Iceberg catalog expects to perform snapshot expiry on its own.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_disable_snapshot_tagging:false	- Whether to disable tagging of Iceberg snapshots. These tags are used to ensure that the snapshots that Redpanda writes are retained during snapshot removal, which in turn, helps Redpanda ensure exactly once delivery of records. Disabling tags is therefore not recommended, but may be useful if the Iceberg catalog does not support tags.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_dlq_table_suffix:~dlq	- Suffix appended to the Iceberg table name for the dead-letter queue (DLQ) table that stores invalid records when the invalid record action is set to `dlq_table`. Should be chosen in a way that avoids name collisions with other Iceberg tables. Important for catalogs which do not support ~ (tilde) in table names. Should not be changed after any DLQ tables have been created.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_enabled:false	- Enables Apache Iceberg integration for storing topic data in the Iceberg open table format. Setting iceberg_enabled to true activates the feature at the cluster level, but each topic must also configure the redpanda.iceberg.mode topic-level property to use it.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_invalid_record_action:dlq_table	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.invalid.record.action topic property.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_latest_schema_cache_ttl_ms:300000ms	- The TTL for the cache in translation that stores the latest schema when using the `value_schema_latest` iceberg mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode:none	- The authentication mode for client requests made to the Iceberg catalog. Choose from: `none`, `bearer`, `oauth2`, and `aws_sigv4`. In `bearer` mode, the token specified in `iceberg_rest_catalog_token` is used unconditonally, and no attempts are made to refresh the token. In `oauth2` mode, the credentials specified in `iceberg_rest_catalog_client_id` and `iceberg_rest_catalog_client_secret` are used to obtain a bearer token from the URI defined by `iceberg_rest_catalog_oauth2_server_uri`. In `aws_sigv4` mode, the same AWS credentials used for cloud storage (see `cloud_storage_region`, `cloud_storage_access_key`, `cloud_storage_secret_key`, and `cloud_storage_credentials_source`) are used to sign requests to AWS Glue catalog with SigV4.In `gcp` mode Redpanda will use VM metadata for authentication.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_access_key:none	- AWS access key for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_access_key when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_region:none	- AWS region for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_region when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_secret_key:none	- AWS secret key for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_secret_key when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_service_name:glue	- AWS service name for SigV4 signing when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode. Defaults to 'glue' for AWS Glue Data Catalog. Can be changed to support other AWS services that provide Iceberg REST catalog APIs.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_base_location:none	- Base URI for the Iceberg REST catalog. If unset, the REST catalog server determines the location. Some REST catalogs, like AWS Glue, require the client to set this. After Iceberg is enabled, do not change this value.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_client_id:none	- Iceberg REST catalog user ID. This ID is used to query the catalog API for the OAuth token. Required if catalog type is set to `rest` and `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `oauth2`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_client_secret:none	- Secret to authenticate against Iceberg REST catalog. Required if catalog type is set to `rest` and `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `oauth2`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_credentials_host:none	- The hostname to connect to for retrieving role based credentials for the Iceberg REST catalog. Derived from iceberg_rest_catalog_credentials_source if not set. Only required when using IAM role based access on AWS; does not apply to OAuth-based authentication schemes. Independent of cloud_storage_credentials_host.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_credentials_source:none	- Source of AWS credentials for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_credentials_source when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode. Accepted values: config_file, aws_instance_metadata, sts, gcp_instance_metadata, azure_vm_instance_metadata, azure_aks_oidc_federation.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_crl:none	- The contents of a certificate revocation list for `iceberg_rest_catalog_trust`. Takes precedence over `iceberg_rest_catalog_crl_file`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_crl_file:none	- Path to certificate revocation list for `iceberg_rest_catalog_trust_file`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_endpoint:none	- URL of Iceberg REST catalog endpoint
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_gcp_user_project:none	- The GCP project that is billed for charges associated with Iceberg REST Catalog requests.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_oauth2_scope:PRINCIPAL_ROLE:ALL	- The OAuth scope used to retrieve access tokens for Iceberg catalog authentication. Only meaningful when `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `oauth2`
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_oauth2_server_uri:none	- The OAuth URI used to retrieve access tokens for Iceberg catalog authentication. If left undefined, the deprecated Iceberg catalog endpoint `/v1/oauth/tokens` is used instead.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_request_timeout_ms:10000ms	- Maximum length of time that Redpanda waits for a response from the REST catalog before aborting the request
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_token:none	- Token used to access the REST Iceberg catalog. Required if `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `bearer`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_trust:none	- The contents of a certificate chain to trust for the REST Iceberg catalog. Takes precedence over `iceberg_rest_catalog_trust_file`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_trust_file:none	- Path to a file containing a certificate chain to trust for the REST Iceberg catalog
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_warehouse:none	- Warehouse to use for the Iceberg REST catalog. Redpanda will query the catalog for configurations specific to the warehouse, for example, using it to automatically configure the appropriate prefix.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_schema_case_insensitive:auto	- Schema field name comparison mode when matching Redpanda's schema against the one returned by the Iceberg catalog. Some catalogs (e.g. AWS Glue) return field names with inconsistent casing, requiring case-insensitive comparison. "auto" enables case-insensitive comparison when the catalog is AWS Glue, and exact comparison otherwise.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_target_backlog_size:104857600	- Total size of the datalake translation backlog that the backlog controller will try to maintain. When a backlog size is larger than the setpoint a backlog controller will increase the translation scheduling group priority.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,156 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_target_lag_ms:60000ms	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.target.lag.ms topic property, which controls how often data in an Iceberg table is refreshed with new data from the corresponding Redpanda topic. Redpanda attempts to commit all the data produced to the topic within the lag target in a best effort fashion, subject to resource availability.
