INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:44,157 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.retention_local_target_capacity_bytes:none	- The target capacity (in bytes) that log storage will try to use before additional retention rules take over to trim data to meet the target. When no target is specified, storage usage is unbounded. Redpanda Data recommends setting only one of `retention_local_target_capacity_bytes` or `retention_local_target_capacity_percent`. If both are set, the minimum of the two is used as the effective target capacity.
