INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.abort_index_segment_size:50000	- Capacity (in number of txns) of an abort index segment. Each partition tracks the aborted transaction offset ranges to help service client requests.If the number transactions increase beyond this threshold, they are flushed to disk to easy memory pressure.Then they're loaded on demand. This configuration controls the maximum number of aborted transactions  before they are flushed to disk.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.abort_timed_out_transactions_interval_ms:10000ms	- Interval, in milliseconds, at which Redpanda looks for inactive transactions and aborts them.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.admin_api_require_auth:false	- Whether Admin API clients must provide HTTP basic authentication headers.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.aggregate_metrics:false	- Enable aggregation of metrics returned by the `/metrics` endpoint. Aggregation can simplify monitoring by providing summarized data instead of raw, per-instance metrics. Metric aggregation is performed by summing the values of samples by labels and is done when it makes sense by the shard and/or partition labels.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.alive_timeout_ms:5000ms	- The amount of time since the last broker status heartbeat. After this time, a broker is considered offline and not alive.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.append_chunk_size:16384	- Size of direct write operations to disk in bytes. A larger chunk size can improve performance for write-heavy workloads, but increase latency for these writes as more data is collected before each write operation. A smaller chunk size can decrease write latency, but potentially increase the number of disk I/O operations.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_client_max_buffer_size:16777216	- Defines the number of bytes allocated by the internal audit client for audit messages. When changing this, you must disable audit logging and then re-enable it for the change to take effect. Consider increasing this if your system generates a very large number of audit records in a short amount of time.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_enabled:false	- Enables or disables audit logging. When you set this to true, Redpanda checks for an existing topic named `_redpanda.audit_log`. If none is found, Redpanda automatically creates one for you.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_enabled_event_types:["management", "authenticate", "admin"]	- List of strings in JSON style identifying the event types to include in the audit log. This may include any of the following: `management, produce, consume, describe, heartbeat, authenticate, schema_registry, admin`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_excluded_principals:[]	- List of user principals to exclude from auditing.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_excluded_topics:[]	- List of topics to exclude from auditing.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_failure_policy:reject	- Defines the policy for rejecting audit log messages when the audit log queue is full. If set to 'permit', then new audit messages are dropped and the operation is permitted.  If set to 'reject', then the operation is rejected.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_log_num_partitions:12	- Defines the number of partitions used by a newly-created audit topic. This configuration applies only to the audit log topic and may be different from the cluster or other topic configurations. This cannot be altered for existing audit log topics.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_log_replication_factor:none	- Defines the replication factor for a newly-created audit log topic. This configuration applies only to the audit log topic and may be different from the cluster or other topic configurations. This cannot be altered for existing audit log topics. Setting this value is optional. If a value is not provided, Redpanda will use the value specified for `internal_topic_replication_factor`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_queue_drain_interval_ms:500ms	- Interval, in milliseconds, at which Redpanda flushes the queued audit log messages to the audit log topic. Longer intervals may help prevent duplicate messages, especially in high throughput scenarios, but they also increase the risk of data loss during shutdowns where the queue is lost.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_queue_max_buffer_size_per_shard:1048576	- Defines the maximum amount of memory in bytes used by the audit buffer in each shard. Once this size is reached, requests to log additional audit messages will return a non-retryable error. Limiting the buffer size per shard helps prevent any single shard from consuming excessive memory due to audit log messages.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.audit_use_rpc:true	- Produce audit log messages using internal Redpanda RPCs. When disabled, produce audit log messages using a Kafka client instead.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.auto_create_topics_enabled:true	- Allow automatic topic creation. To prevent excess topics, this property is not supported on Redpanda Cloud BYOC and Dedicated clusters. You should explicitly manage topic creation for these Redpanda Cloud clusters. If you produce to a topic that doesn't exist, the topic will be created with defaults if this property is enabled.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_io_admission_control_policy:reservation	- Selects the admission policy used by cloud_io::admission_control. 'passthrough' disables admission control (client pool is the only constraint). 'reservation' introduces reserved-slot admission control, configurable across a fixed set of groups: producer_upload, consumer_fetch, and default_group.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_io_admission_control_reservation:["producer_upload:2", "consumer_fetch:2", "metastore:2", "default_group:2"]	- Per-group target_reserved values for the reservation_policy admission control. Each entry has the form 'group_name:slots' (e.g. 'producer_upload:2'). The policy keeps each group's reservation lane sized to this target while the group is active; idle reservations past the dwell window are reclaimed back to the common pool. Entries with an unrecognized group name are rejected when the property is set. Only consulted when cloud_io_admission_control_policy=reservation.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_access_key:none	- AWS or GCP access key. This access key is part of the credentials that Redpanda requires to authenticate with object storage services for Tiered Storage. This access key is used with the <<cloud_storage_secret_key>> to form the complete credentials required for authentication. To authenticate using IAM roles, see cloud_storage_credentials_source.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_api_endpoint:none	- Optional API endpoint. - AWS: When blank, this is automatically generated using <<cloud_storage_region,region>> and <<cloud_storage_bucket,bucket>>. Otherwise, this uses the value assigned. - GCP: Uses `storage.googleapis.com`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_api_endpoint_port:443	- TLS port override.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_attempt_cluster_restore_on_bootstrap:false	- When set to `true`, Redpanda automatically retrieves cluster metadata from a specified object storage bucket at the cluster's first startup. This option is ideal for orchestrated deployments, such as Kubernetes. Ensure any previous cluster linked to the bucket is fully decommissioned to prevent conflicts between Tiered Storage subsystems.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_azure_adls_endpoint:none	- Azure Data Lake Storage v2 endpoint override. Use when hierarchical namespaces are enabled on your storage account and you have set up a custom endpoint.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_azure_adls_port:none	- Azure Data Lake Storage v2 port override. See also `cloud_storage_azure_adls_endpoint`. Use when Hierarchical Namespaces are enabled on your storage account and you have set up a custom endpoint.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_azure_container:none	- The name of the Azure container to use with Tiered Storage. If `null`, the property is disabled. The container must belong to cloud_storage_azure_storage_account.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_azure_hierarchical_namespace_enabled:none	- Whether or not an Azure hierarchical namespace is enabled on the `cloud_storage_azure_storage_account`. If this property is not set, ´cloud_storage_azure_shared_key` must be set, and each node tries to determine at startup if a hierarchical namespace is enabled. Setting this property to `true` disables the check and treats a hierarchical namespace as active. Setting to `false` disables the check and treats a hierarchical namespace as not active.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_azure_managed_identity_id:none	- The managed identity ID to use for access to the Azure storage account. To use Azure managed identities, you must set `cloud_storage_credentials_source` to `azure_vm_instance_metadata`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_azure_shared_key:none	- The shared key to be used for Azure Shared Key authentication with the Azure storage account configured by `cloud_storage_azure_storage_account`.  If `null`, the property is disabled. Redpanda expects this key string to be Base64 encoded.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_azure_storage_account:none	- The name of the Azure storage account to use with Tiered Storage. If `null`, the property is disabled.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_backend:unknown	- Optional object storage backend variant used to select API capabilities. If not supplied, this will be inferred from other configuration properties.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_background_jobs_quota:5000	- The total number of requests the object storage background jobs can make during one background housekeeping run. This is a per-shard limit. Adjusting this limit can optimize object storage traffic and impact shard performance.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_bucket:none	- AWS or GCP bucket or container that should be used to store data.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_check_interval:5000ms	- Minimum interval between Tiered Storage cache trims, measured in milliseconds. This setting dictates the cooldown period after a cache trim operation before another trim can occur. If a cache fetch operation requests a trim but the interval since the last trim has not yet passed, the trim will be postponed until this cooldown expires. Adjusting this interval helps manage the balance between cache size and retrieval performance.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_chunk_size:16777216	- Size of chunks of segments downloaded into object storage cache. Reduces space usage by only downloading the necessary chunk from a segment.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_max_objects:100000	- Maximum number of objects that may be held in the Tiered Storage cache.  This applies simultaneously with `cloud_storage_cache_size`, and whichever limit is hit first will trigger trimming of the cache.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_num_buckets:0	- Divide the object storage cache across the specified number of buckets. This only works for objects with randomized prefixes. The names are not changed when the value is set to zero.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_size:0	- Maximum size of object storage cache. If both this property and cloud_storage_cache_size_percent are set, Redpanda uses the minimum of the two.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_size_percent:optional(20)	- Maximum size of the cloud cache as a percentage of unreserved disk space disk_reservation_percent. The default value for this option is tuned for a shared disk configuration. Consider increasing the value if using a dedicated cache disk. The property <<cloud_storage_cache_size,`cloud_storage_cache_size`>> controls the same limit expressed as a fixed number of bytes. If both `cloud_storage_cache_size` and `cloud_storage_cache_size_percent` are set, Redpanda uses the minimum of the two.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_trim_carryover_bytes:0	- The cache performs a recursive directory inspection during the cache trim. The information obtained during the inspection can be carried over to the next trim operation. This parameter sets a limit on the memory occupied by objects that can be carried over from one trim to next, and allows cache to quickly unblock readers before starting the directory inspection (deprecated)
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_trim_threshold_percent_objects:none	- Trim is triggered when the cache reaches this percent of the maximum object count. If this is unset, the default behavioris to start trim when the cache is about 100% full.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_trim_threshold_percent_size:none	- Trim is triggered when the cache reaches this percent of the maximum cache size. If this is unset, the default behavioris to start trim when the cache is about 100% full.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cache_trim_walk_concurrency:1	- The maximum number of concurrent tasks launched for directory walk during cache trimming. A higher number allows cache trimming to run faster but can cause latency spikes due to increased pressure on I/O subsystem and syscall threads.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_chunk_eviction_strategy:eager	- Selects a strategy for evicting unused cache chunks.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_chunk_prefetch:0	- Number of chunks to prefetch ahead of every downloaded chunk
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_client_lease_timeout_ms:900000ms	- Maximum time to hold a cloud storage client lease (ms), after which any outstanding connection is immediately closed.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cluster_metadata_num_consumer_groups_per_upload:1000	- Number of groups to upload in a single snapshot object during consumer offsets upload. Setting a lower value will mean a larger number of smaller snapshots are uploaded.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cluster_metadata_retries:5	- Number of attempts metadata operations may be retried.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cluster_metadata_upload_interval_ms:3600000ms	- Time interval to wait between cluster metadata uploads.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cluster_metadata_upload_timeout_ms:60000ms	- Timeout for cluster metadata uploads.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_cluster_name:none	- Optional unique name to disambiguate this cluster's metadata in object storage (e.g. for Whole Cluster Restore) when multiple clusters share a bucket. Must be unique within the bucket, 1-64 chars, [A-Za-z0-9_-]. Do not change once set.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_credentials_host:none	- The hostname to connect to for retrieving role based credentials. Derived from cloud_storage_credentials_source if not set. Only required when using IAM role based access. To authenticate using access keys, see `cloud_storage_access_key`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_credentials_source:config_file	- The source of credentials used to authenticate to object storage services. Required for cluster provider authentication with IAM roles. To authenticate using access keys, see cloud_storage_access_key`. Accepted values: `config_file`, `aws_instance_metadata`, `sts, gcp_instance_metadata`, `azure_vm_instance_metadata`, `azure_aks_oidc_federation` 
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_crl_file:none	- Path to certificate revocation list for `cloud_storage_trust_file`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_disable_archival_stm_rw_fence:false	- Disable concurrency control mechanism in the Tiered-Storage. This could potentially break the metadata consistency and shouldn't be used in production systems. It should only be used for testing.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_disable_archiver_manager:true	- Use legacy upload mode and do not start archiver_manager.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,198 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.cloud_storage_disable_chunk_reads:false	- Disable chunk reads and switch back to legacy mode where full segments are downloaded.
