INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_listoffsets_historical_leader_epoch:false	- When enabled, the Kafka ListOffsets API returns the historical (record-time) leader epoch instead of the current leader epoch. Intended as a one-way opt-in: disabling after it has been enabled regresses to the original bug. Gated as a development feature: not all response paths are fixed yet (CORE-12505), so enabling this property produces internally inconsistent epoch values across paths and must not be enabled in production.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_metrics_reporter:true	- Enable the cluster metrics reporter. If `true`, the metrics reporter collects and exports to Redpanda Data a set of customer usage metrics at the interval set by `metrics_reporter_report_interval`. The cluster metrics of the metrics reporter are different from the monitoring metrics. * The metrics reporter exports customer usage metrics for consumption by Redpanda Data.* Monitoring metrics are exported for consumption by Redpanda users.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_mpx_extensions:false	- Enable Redpanda extensions for MPX.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_pid_file:true	- Enable PID file. You should not need to change.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_rack_awareness:false	- Enable rack-aware replica assignment.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_sasl:false	- Enable SASL authentication for Kafka connections. Authorization is required to modify this property. See also `kafka_enable_authorization`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_schema_id_validation:none	- Mode to enable server-side schema ID validation. Accepted Values: * `none`: Schema validation is disabled (no schema ID checks are done). Associated topic properties cannot be modified. * `redpanda`: Schema validation is enabled. Only Redpanda topic properties are accepted. * `compat`: Schema validation is enabled. Both Redpanda and compatible topic properties are accepted.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_shadow_linking:false	- Enable creating Shadow Links from this cluster to a remote source cluster for data replication.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_transactions:true	- Enable transactions (atomic writes).
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_usage:false	- Enables the usage tracking mechanism, storing windowed history of kafka/cloud_storage metrics over time.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.features_auto_enable:true	- Whether features whose `available_policy` is `always` or `new_clusters_only` are auto-activated by the controller after the cluster active logical version reaches their required version. When false, the cluster active version still advances normally, but each such feature must be activated explicitly via the Admin API. Does not affect features with `available_policy::explicit_only`, which always require explicit activation.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.features_auto_finalization:true	- Whether the cluster active logical version is advanced automatically once all nodes have been upgraded (true), or only in response to an explicit request via the Admin API (false). When false, the cluster remains able to downgrade to the previous version until finalization is requested. Setting this to false is an Enterprise feature and requires a valid license. Note: if upgrade was performed with this set to false and the cluster is ready to finalize, flipping this to true does not reliably trigger finalization. Leave this set to false and use the Admin API to finalize; once the upgrade is complete this can be set back to true to restore automatic finalization for future upgrades.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_max_bytes:57671680	- Maximum number of bytes returned in a fetch request.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_max_read_concurrency:1	- The maximum number of concurrent partition reads per fetch request on each shard. Setting this higher than the default can lead to partition starvation and unneeded memory usage.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_pid_d_coeff:0	- Derivative coefficient for fetch PID controller.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_pid_i_coeff:0.01	- Integral coefficient for fetch PID controller.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_pid_max_debounce_ms:100ms	- The maximum debounce time the fetch PID controller will apply, in milliseconds.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_pid_p_coeff:100	- Proportional coefficient for fetch PID controller.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_pid_target_utilization_fraction:0.2	- A fraction, between 0 and 1, for the target reactor utilization of the fetch scheduling group.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_read_strategy:non_polling	- The strategy used to fulfill fetch requests. * `polling`: If `fetch_reads_debounce_timeout` is set to its default value, then this acts exactly like `non_polling`; otherwise, it acts like `non_polling_with_debounce` (deprecated). * `non_polling`: The backend is signaled when a partition has new data, so Redpanda does not need to repeatedly read from every partition in the fetch. Redpanda Data recommends using this value for most workloads, because it can improve fetch latency and CPU utilization. * `non_polling_with_debounce`: This option behaves like `non_polling`, but it includes a debounce mechanism with a fixed delay specified by `fetch_reads_debounce_timeout` at the start of each fetch. By introducing this delay, Redpanda can accumulate more data before processing, leading to fewer fetch operations and returning larger amounts of data. Enabling this option reduces reactor utilization, but it may also increase end-to-end latency.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_reads_debounce_timeout:10ms	- Time to wait for the next read in fetch requests when the requested minimum bytes was not reached.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.fetch_session_eviction_timeout_ms:60000ms	- Time duration after which the inactive fetch session is removed from the fetch session cache. Fetch sessions are used to implement the incremental fetch requests where a consumer does not send all requested partitions to the server but the server tracks them for the consumer.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.group_initial_rebalance_delay:0ms	- Delay added to the rebalance phase to wait for new members.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.group_max_session_timeout_ms:300000ms	- The maximum allowed session timeout for registered consumers. Longer timeouts give consumers more time to process messages in between heartbeats at the cost of a longer time to detect failures.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.group_min_session_timeout_ms:6000ms	- The minimum allowed session timeout for registered consumers. Shorter timeouts result in quicker failure detection at the cost of more frequent consumer heartbeating, which can overwhelm broker resources.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.group_new_member_join_timeout:30000ms	- Timeout for new member joins.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.group_offset_retention_check_ms:600000ms	- Frequency rate at which the system should check for expired group offsets.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.group_offset_retention_sec:optional(604800s)	- Consumer group offset retention seconds. To disable offset retention, set this to null.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.group_topic_partitions:3	- Number of partitions in the internal group membership topic.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.health_manager_tick_interval:180000ms	- How often the health manager runs.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.health_monitor_max_metadata_age:10000ms	- Maximum age of the metadata cached in the health monitor of a non-controller broker.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.health_monitor_metrics_enabled:false	- Whether the cluster_health_* metrics are exported. When enabled, each broker refreshes them on an interval of 10x `health_monitor_max_metadata_age`, so the two scale together. Refreshing increases CPU usage and network traffic. Disabled by default.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.health_monitor_tick_interval:10000ms	- How often health monitor refresh cluster state
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.http_authentication:["BASIC"]	- A list of supported HTTP authentication mechanisms. Accepted Values: `BASIC`, `OIDC`
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_backlog_controller_i_coeff:0.005	- Integral coefficient for the Iceberg backlog controller. The error is integrated (accumulated) over time and the aggregated value contributes to the datalake translation priority with this coefficient.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_backlog_controller_p_coeff:1e-05	- Proportional coefficient for the Iceberg backlog controller. Number of shares assigned to the datalake scheduling group will be proportional to the backlog size error.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_base_location:redpanda-iceberg-catalog	- Base path for the cloud-storage-object-backed Iceberg filesystem catalog. After Iceberg is enabled, do not change this value.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_commit_interval_ms:60000ms	- The frequency at which the Iceberg coordinator commits topic files to the catalog. This is the interval between commit transactions across all topics monitored by the coordinator, not the interval between individual commits.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_type:object_storage	- Iceberg catalog type that Redpanda will use to commit table metadata updates. Supported types: 'rest', 'object_storage'
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_default_catalog_namespace:["redpanda"]	- The default namespace (database name) for Iceberg tables. All tables created by Redpanda will be placed in this namespace within the Iceberg catalog. Supports nested namespaces as an array of strings. IMPORTANT: This value must be configured before enabling Iceberg and must not be changed afterward. Changing it will cause Redpanda to lose track of existing tables.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_default_partition_spec:(hour(redpanda.timestamp))	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.partition.spec topic property that determines the partition spec for the Iceberg table corresponding to the topic. If this property is not set and AWS Glue is being used as the Iceberg REST catalog, the default value will be overridden by an empty partition spec, for compatibility with AWS Glue.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_delete:true	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.delete topic property that determines if the corresponding Iceberg table is deleted upon deleting the topic.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_disable_automatic_snapshot_expiry:false	- Whether to disable automatic Iceberg snapshot expiry. This may be useful if the Iceberg catalog expects to perform snapshot expiry on its own.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_disable_snapshot_tagging:false	- Whether to disable tagging of Iceberg snapshots. These tags are used to ensure that the snapshots that Redpanda writes are retained during snapshot removal, which in turn, helps Redpanda ensure exactly once delivery of records. Disabling tags is therefore not recommended, but may be useful if the Iceberg catalog does not support tags.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_dlq_table_suffix:~dlq	- Suffix appended to the Iceberg table name for the dead-letter queue (DLQ) table that stores invalid records when the invalid record action is set to `dlq_table`. Should be chosen in a way that avoids name collisions with other Iceberg tables. Important for catalogs which do not support ~ (tilde) in table names. Should not be changed after any DLQ tables have been created.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_enabled:false	- Enables Apache Iceberg integration for storing topic data in the Iceberg open table format. Setting iceberg_enabled to true activates the feature at the cluster level, but each topic must also configure the redpanda.iceberg.mode topic-level property to use it.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_invalid_record_action:dlq_table	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.invalid.record.action topic property.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_latest_schema_cache_ttl_ms:300000ms	- The TTL for the cache in translation that stores the latest schema when using the `value_schema_latest` iceberg mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode:none	- The authentication mode for client requests made to the Iceberg catalog. Choose from: `none`, `bearer`, `oauth2`, and `aws_sigv4`. In `bearer` mode, the token specified in `iceberg_rest_catalog_token` is used unconditonally, and no attempts are made to refresh the token. In `oauth2` mode, the credentials specified in `iceberg_rest_catalog_client_id` and `iceberg_rest_catalog_client_secret` are used to obtain a bearer token from the URI defined by `iceberg_rest_catalog_oauth2_server_uri`. In `aws_sigv4` mode, the same AWS credentials used for cloud storage (see `cloud_storage_region`, `cloud_storage_access_key`, `cloud_storage_secret_key`, and `cloud_storage_credentials_source`) are used to sign requests to AWS Glue catalog with SigV4.In `gcp` mode Redpanda will use VM metadata for authentication.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_access_key:none	- AWS access key for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_access_key when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_region:none	- AWS region for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_region when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_secret_key:none	- AWS secret key for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_secret_key when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_aws_service_name:glue	- AWS service name for SigV4 signing when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode. Defaults to 'glue' for AWS Glue Data Catalog. Can be changed to support other AWS services that provide Iceberg REST catalog APIs.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_base_location:none	- Base URI for the Iceberg REST catalog. If unset, the REST catalog server determines the location. Some REST catalogs, like AWS Glue, require the client to set this. After Iceberg is enabled, do not change this value.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_client_id:none	- Iceberg REST catalog user ID. This ID is used to query the catalog API for the OAuth token. Required if catalog type is set to `rest` and `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `oauth2`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_client_secret:none	- Secret to authenticate against Iceberg REST catalog. Required if catalog type is set to `rest` and `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `oauth2`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_credentials_host:none	- The hostname to connect to for retrieving role based credentials for the Iceberg REST catalog. Derived from iceberg_rest_catalog_credentials_source if not set. Only required when using IAM role based access on AWS; does not apply to OAuth-based authentication schemes. Independent of cloud_storage_credentials_host.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_credentials_source:none	- Source of AWS credentials for Iceberg REST catalog SigV4 authentication. If not set, falls back to cloud_storage_credentials_source when using aws_sigv4 authentication mode. Accepted values: config_file, aws_instance_metadata, sts, gcp_instance_metadata, azure_vm_instance_metadata, azure_aks_oidc_federation.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_crl:none	- The contents of a certificate revocation list for `iceberg_rest_catalog_trust`. Takes precedence over `iceberg_rest_catalog_crl_file`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_crl_file:none	- Path to certificate revocation list for `iceberg_rest_catalog_trust_file`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_endpoint:none	- URL of Iceberg REST catalog endpoint
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_gcp_user_project:none	- The GCP project that is billed for charges associated with Iceberg REST Catalog requests.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_oauth2_scope:PRINCIPAL_ROLE:ALL	- The OAuth scope used to retrieve access tokens for Iceberg catalog authentication. Only meaningful when `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `oauth2`
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_oauth2_server_uri:none	- The OAuth URI used to retrieve access tokens for Iceberg catalog authentication. If left undefined, the deprecated Iceberg catalog endpoint `/v1/oauth/tokens` is used instead.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_request_timeout_ms:10000ms	- Maximum length of time that Redpanda waits for a response from the REST catalog before aborting the request
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_token:none	- Token used to access the REST Iceberg catalog. Required if `iceberg_rest_catalog_authentication_mode` is set to `bearer`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_trust:none	- The contents of a certificate chain to trust for the REST Iceberg catalog. Takes precedence over `iceberg_rest_catalog_trust_file`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_trust_file:none	- Path to a file containing a certificate chain to trust for the REST Iceberg catalog
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_rest_catalog_warehouse:none	- Warehouse to use for the Iceberg REST catalog. Redpanda will query the catalog for configurations specific to the warehouse, for example, using it to automatically configure the appropriate prefix.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_schema_case_insensitive:auto	- Schema field name comparison mode when matching Redpanda's schema against the one returned by the Iceberg catalog. Some catalogs (e.g. AWS Glue) return field names with inconsistent casing, requiring case-insensitive comparison. "auto" enables case-insensitive comparison when the catalog is AWS Glue, and exact comparison otherwise.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_target_backlog_size:104857600	- Total size of the datalake translation backlog that the backlog controller will try to maintain. When a backlog size is larger than the setpoint a backlog controller will increase the translation scheduling group priority.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_target_lag_ms:60000ms	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.target.lag.ms topic property, which controls how often data in an Iceberg table is refreshed with new data from the corresponding Redpanda topic. Redpanda attempts to commit all the data produced to the topic within the lag target in a best effort fashion, subject to resource availability.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_throttle_backlog_size_ratio:none	- Ratio of total backlog size to disk space that triggers throttling for Iceberg producers. Set to `null` to disable throttling.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_topic_name_dot_replacement:none	- Optional replacement string for dots in topic names when deriving Iceberg table names, useful when downstream systems do not permit dots in table names. The replacement string cannot contain dots. Be careful to avoid table name collisions caused by the replacement.If an Iceberg topic with dots in the name exists in the cluster, the value of this property should not be changed.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.id_allocator_batch_size:1000	- The ID allocator allocates messages in batches (each batch is a one log record) and then serves requests from memory without touching the log until the batch is exhausted.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.id_allocator_log_capacity:100	- Capacity of the `id_allocator` log in number of batches. After it reaches `id_allocator_stm`, it truncates the log's prefix.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.initial_retention_local_target_bytes_default:none	- Initial local retention size target for partitions of topics with Tiered Storage enabled. If no initial local target retention is configured all locally retained data will be delivered to learner when joining partition replica set.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.initial_retention_local_target_ms_default:none	- Initial local retention time target for partitions of topics with Tiered Storage enabled. If no initial local target retention is configured all locally retained data will be delivered to learner when joining partition replica set.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.internal_rpc_request_timeout_ms:10000ms	- Default timeout for RPC requests between Redpanda nodes.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.internal_topic_replication_factor:3	- Target replication factor for internal topics.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.join_retry_timeout_ms:5000ms	- Time between cluster join retries in milliseconds.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_batch_max_bytes:1048576	- Maximum size of a batch processed by the server. If the batch is compressed, the limit applies to the compressed batch size.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_connection_rate_limit:none	- Maximum connections per second for one core. If `null` (the default), then the number of connections per second is unlimited.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_connection_rate_limit_overrides:[]	- Overrides the maximum connections per second for one core for the specified IP addresses (for example, `['127.0.0.1:90', '50.20.1.1:40']`)
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_connections_max:none	- Maximum number of Kafka client connections per broker. If `null`, the property is disabled.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_connections_max_overrides:[]	- A list of IP addresses for which Kafka client connection limits are overridden and don't apply. For example, `(['127.0.0.1:90', '50.20.1.1:40']).`
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_connections_max_per_ip:none	- Maximum number of Kafka client connections per IP address, per broker. If `null`, the property is disabled.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_enable_authorization:none	- Flag to require authorization for Kafka connections. If `null`, the property is disabled, and authorization is instead enabled by enable_sasl. * `null`: Ignored. Authorization is enabled with `enable_sasl`: `true` * `true`: authorization is required. * `false`: authorization is disabled.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:10:13,199 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.kafka_enable_describe_log_dirs_remote_storage:true	- Whether to include Tiered Storage as a special remote:// directory in `DescribeLogDirs Kafka` API requests.
